.\" Man page for winder
.TH WINDER 1 "August 2026" "Winder 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
winder \- native WINGs file manager for Window Maker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B winder
.RI [ directory ]
.br
.B winder
.BR \-h | \-\-help
.br
.B winder
.BR \-V | \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B winder
is a Finder-inspired file manager built with the WINGs toolkit used by
Window Maker. It provides a favorites sidebar, a list view with sortable
headers (the default on start), NeXT-style column browsing, Get Info
previews (text, images, folders), a right-click context menu, and basic
file operations (open, rename, delete, duplicate, compress, copy/paste,
open terminal).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I directory
Open this directory on startup. Defaults to the user's home directory.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH KEYBOARD
When focus is on a browse surface (file list, column browser, or sidebar),
not the path or Find fields:
.TP
.B Up/Down
Move the selection.
.TP
.B Left/Right
In columns: go to the parent column or open a folder. In list view: go back
or open the selection.
.TP
.B /
Focus the Find field.
.TP
.B Escape
Return focus to the file view.
.TP
.B Enter
Open the selection.
.TP
.B Mouse Back / Forward
Side buttons on many mice (X11 buttons 8 and 9) move history back and
forward, same as the toolbar
.B <
and
.B >
buttons.
.SH CONTEXT MENU
Right-click a file, folder, or empty area in the column or list view.
Item actions include Open, Open in New Window (folders only), Rename,
Duplicate, Delete, Compress, Copy, Copy Path, Paste, and Open Terminal Here.
Background actions operate on the current folder (for example New Folder,
Paste, Terminal).
.SH FILES
No configuration files are used yet. Sidebar favorites are derived from the
user's home directory and common paths.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wmaker (1),
.BR xdg-open (1)
